fix(shim): relax --force-with-lease on feature branches; refuse only on protected

Per-operator direction 2026-05-22: plain --force / -f refused on every branch (unsafe), but --force-with-lease (race-safe) is the standard feature-branch rebase finisher and should not require PD_SHIM_OFF=1 every time.

New logic: scan argv for plain-force vs lease-force separately; combine with the protected-target detection. plain-force → push-force (refused anywhere). lease-force + protected (main/master/release/*) → push-force-lease-protected (refused). lease-force + feature → falls through (allowed). Plain push to protected without force → push-protected (refused; PR instead). All 5,813 unit tests pass.


